artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $d\geq 1$ and consider the semiclassical Schrödinger operator $H_\hbar = -\hbar^2\Delta + V$ on $L^2(\mathbb{R}^d)$ with a (possibly complex-valued) potential $V$ such that $\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}|V(x)|^{\gamma+d/2}\,dx<\infty$ for some $\gamma>0$. Let $\{E_j\}$ denote the discrete eigenvalues of $H_\hbar$ in $\mathbb{C}\setminus[0,\infty)$ (counted with algebraic multiplicity), and define the distance to the essential spectrum
$$\delta(E) := \mathrm{dist}(E, [0,\infty)).$$
Consider nonlocal scale-invariant eigenvalue inequalities of the form
$$\sum_j |E_j|^{\alpha}\left(\frac{\delta(E_j)}{|E_j|}\right)^{\beta} \;\le\; C_{\alpha,\beta,\gamma,d}\left(\hbar^{-d}\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}|V(x)|^{\gamma+d/2}\,dx\right)^{\alpha/\gamma}, \qquad (\star)$$
where the sum is restricted to eigenvalues satisfying the truncation specified below. The following six parameter regimes are known to yield $(\star)$:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] $\alpha=1/2$, $\beta=1$, $0<\gamma<d/(2(2d-1))$, $d\geq 2$, no truncation;
\item[(b)] $\alpha>(d-1)\gamma/(d/2-\gamma)$, $\beta=1$, $d/(2(2d-1))\le \gamma\le 1/2$, $d\geq 2$, no truncation;
\item[(c)] $\alpha=\beta>2\gamma$, $\gamma>1/2$, summing only over $j$ with $|E_j|^\gamma\le \hbar^{-d}\int|V|^{\gamma+d/2}$;
\item[(d)] $0<\alpha<\gamma(\gamma+d/2)$, $\beta>2\gamma$, $\gamma>1/2$, summing only over $j$ with $|E_j|^\gamma\ge \hbar^{-d}\int|V|^{\gamma+d/2}$;
\item[(e)] $\alpha=\beta=\gamma+d/2$, with $\gamma\geq 1/2$ if $d=1$ and $\gamma>0$ if $d\geq 2$, summing over $j$ with $|E_j|^\gamma\le \hbar^{-d}\int|V|^{\gamma+d/2}$;
\item[(f)] $\alpha>\gamma$, $\beta=\gamma+d/2$, with $\gamma\geq 1/2$ if $d=1$ and $\gamma>0$ if $d\geq 2$, summing over $j$ with $|E_j|^\gamma\ge \hbar^{-d}\int|V|^{\gamma+d/2}$.
\end{itemize}
Determine, in each of the regimes (a)–(f), for which values of $d$, $\alpha$, $\beta$, $\gamma$ the inequality $(\star)$ is sharp up to a factor of $\hbar^{\varepsilon}$ for every $\varepsilon>0$ (in the semiclassical limit $\hbar\to 0^+$). Furthermore, determine whether the parameter region of $(d,\alpha,\beta,\gamma)$ for which a bound of the form $(\star)$ holds can be enlarged beyond the union of (a)–(f).

